            <title><![CDATA[Why the U.S. job market remains resilient in face of global pressures and inflation]]></title>
            <link>https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/why-the-u-s-job-market-remains-resilient-in-face-of-global-pressures-and-inflation</link>
            <description><![CDATA[The job market delivered a surprising rebound in August, adding 162,000 jobs, far more than economists had expected. The unemployment rate held steady at 4.1%, and the Labor Department revised July numbers upward. The stronger-than-expected report comes as the Federal Reserve is set to weigh interest rates. Geoff Bennett discussed more with Roben Farzad, host of "Full Disclosure."]]></description>
